# Secrets — never commit. Keys live here, not in chat, code, or docs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# The demo page is its OWN repository and its own deployment.
#
#   github.com/TheSuperShyy/homies-voice-demo  ->  Vercel
#
# Nested here because that is where it is worked on, but committing it into this
# repo would either swallow its history or leave a broken submodule pointer.
# Push it from inside web/ — `cd web && git push` — not from here.
web/

# Real resident data. sheets/residents.csv IS committed and stays committed —
# it is ten invented people and it is the fixture the whole demo runs on. Any
# other CSV in here is presumed real until proven otherwise, because the one
# produced from a live OXS collection report carries real names against real
# debts, and that is the file nobody would notice going public.
sheets/*.csv
!sheets/residents.csv
*-real.csv

# Same rule, different shape. The arrears sweep writes every resident OXS says
# is behind — name, mobile, building, apartment, months owed, amount. The
# 2026 run held 740 real numbers. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. The scripts that
# produce these files are committed and are the useful part; their output is
# a debtors list and belongs nowhere near GitHub.
docs/reference/arrears-*.json

# OXS's own API documentation. No credentials in it, but it is their internal
# surface and not ours to publish. Keep it local.
OXS_External_API_v1.pdf

# Next.js incremental typecheck cache
dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Other clients worked on from this desktop. Not Homies, not this repo.
Lotosclean-*

# Voice recordings — a person's voice, dropped in for reference or for cloning.
#
# `New Recording 154.m4a (1).mp4` landed in the project root on 5 Aug and was
# untracked but NOT ignored, which meant the next `git add -A` would have pushed
# 3.5 minutes of somebody's speech to GitHub. It missed the 10:xx commit by
# minutes, and that was luck rather than anything working.
#
# A voice recording is biometric-adjacent: it identifies a person, and once it is
# in a repo's history removing it is a rewrite, not a delete. Call recordings from
# Vapi carry a resident on the other end of them too. None of it belongs here.
# Keep them local, or in a store with access control — never in git.
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg
*.opus
*.flac
*.aac
*.webm
# Phone recorders name their exports .m4a and Windows appends .mp4 on download,
# so the extension alone does not catch it.
New Recording*
*.m4a*

# Scratch
tmp/
*.log
# A dump of whatever system prompt was live when someone last debugged a call.
# Stale the moment it is written, and the real one lives in docs/ — two copies
# of a prompt is how they drift.
scripts/_live_prompt.txt

# Chatwoot production secrets — server only
deploy/chatwoot/.env

# Dashboard local env
dashboard/.env.local
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/.next/

# Written by `vercel link` on first deploy. Project and org IDs, not secrets,
# but they tie this checkout to one Vercel account and do not belong in git.
dashboard/.vercel/
